+## smelt functions (only if the spec requires `smelt.define`)
+
+Functions live in a `functions/` directory under the project root — no `smelt.yml` change needed.
+The call path mirrors the file path (without `.sql`):
+
+| File | Call path |
+|------|-----------|
+| `functions/util.sql` → `fn my_fn` | `smelt.functions.util.my_fn(arg)` |
+| `functions/revenue.sql` → `fn safe_revenue` | `smelt.functions.revenue.safe_revenue(arg)` |
+
+Minimal function definition (parameters are `Expr<T>`; return type required):
+
+```sql
+smelt.define is_shipped(status: Expr<Text>) -> Expr<Boolean> AS (
+    status = 'shipped'
+)
+```
+
+**Expression placement:** `Expr<T>`-returning functions are ordinary SQL expressions — they work
+in `SELECT`, `WHERE`, `HAVING`, `CASE WHEN`, and `JOIN ON` conditions, not only in `SELECT` lists.
+Arguments are **positional** (named `param => value` is not yet wired end-to-end). A single
+`.sql` file may contain multiple `smelt.define` declarations.
+
+After defining a function, use `smelt build --show-plan models/<model>.sql` to confirm the call
+expands correctly before doing a full build.
+
